.TH TLLAMAD 1 "October 2026" "TLlama" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tllamad \- foreground TLlama inference daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tllamad
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tllamad
.RI [ options ] " rebuildrepo " [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tllamad
serves model APIs and supervises private native tllama-server workers.
It stays in the foreground. The Debian package supplies tllamad.service.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --config FILE
Select a server TOML configuration file explicitly.
.TP
.B --no-config
Skip configuration-file discovery.
.TP
.B --check-config
Validate the effective configuration and exit without starting a server.
.TP
.B --print-config
Print effective configuration values and their sources, then exit.
.TP
.B --host ADDRESS
Listener address. Default: 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.B --port PORT
Listener port. Default: 54800.
.TP
.B --models-dir DIRECTORY
Model repository root. Default: /var/lib/tllama/models.
.TP
.B --runtime-path FILE
Absolute path to the private native runtime executable.
.TP
.B --device DEVICE
Global default native device selection.
.TP
.B --backend-priority LIST
Comma-separated backend priority.
.TP
.B --help
Show all options and corresponding environment variables.
.TP
.B --version
Show the installed daemon version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Global precedence is command line, environment, server TOML, built-in defaults.
File selection is --config, TLLAMA_CONFIG, the user's tllama/server.toml under
XDG_CONFIG_HOME (or ~/.config), then /etc/tllama/server.toml.
The first existing default file is used, without merging files.
Relative paths use the daemon's working directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/tllama/server.toml
System service configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/tllama/models
Default model repository.
.TP
.I /var/cache/tllama/huggingface
Hugging Face cache used by the packaged service.
.TP
.I /run/tllama
Private worker runtime directory used by the packaged service.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/tllama/server/tllama-server
Native runtime supplied by the separate tllama-server package.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tllama (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
